:: Restart {"position":"300,100","size":"100,100"}
First Day of School

[[START]]


:: START {"position":"300,250","size":"100,100"}
<img src="pic 4.png" style= " max-width:350px; ">
You wake up to the sound of your alarm buzzing off earlier than you’d like. For a moment, you lie still, staring at the ceiling before realizing that today is the first day of school. You couldn’t sleep at all thinking about today. You looked at the time, your face full of exhaustion. 

[[Check your phone]]




:: The bell rings {"position":"300,1700","size":"100,100"}
The bell rings at the end of class. As you pack your bag, you pause for a moment and look around the room. The desks feel more familiar now. The faces are less intimidating. You think back on the day, from the alarm, the hesitation, the awkward conversations, the moments you didn’t plan for. None of your choices led to a perfect outcome, but every single one taught you something. You step into the hallway, realizing that the pressure you felt on Monday is gone. Not because everything went right, but because you learned how to keep going anyway.

The first day of school isn’t about making the best choices.
It’s about realizing that even uncertain choices can move you forward.
Confidence isn’t something you start with; it’s something you build mistake by mistake, choice by choice, decision by decision.
<img src="pic 15.png" style= " max-width:350px; ">
[[Restart]] 


:: You get into your group. {"position":"300,1425","size":"100,100"}
You get into your group and you thought about what first impression you'd like to leave.

''What will you do?''
<img src="pic 1.png" style= " max-width:350px; ">

[[→ Break the ice]]
[[→ Let it happen naturally]]
[[→ Become the leader]]


:: You heard footsteps {"position":"300,800","size":"100,100"}
The classroom slowly starts to quiet down as footsteps approach the door. Someone screams, “The teacher is coming!” Everyone put away their phones, and conversations stopped. She first introduced themselves and began to ask each student to do the same. 

Then she says something unexpected.

“Now you won’t be introducing yourself,” she says. “You’ll introduce the person sitting next to you.”
<img src="pic 7.png" style= " max-width:350px; ">

[[Your heart skips a beat.]] 


:: You listened and waited until everyone has finished with their introduction. {"position":"300,1125","size":"100,100"}
The teacher starts the lesson, and she immediately assigns group work so that everyone can get to know each other more. 
<img src="pic 10.PNG" style= " max-width:350px; ">
[[Find out your group]]


:: You took a glance around your classroom {"position":"300,600","size":"100,100"}
No matter how you arrived, you end up sitting inside the same classroom. The room buzzes with energy. Some students are confident, some are clearly nervous. You glance around, wondering how some people make it look so easy. 

''You hesitate, then decide what to do next. ''
<img src="pic 1.png" style= " max-width:350px; ">

[[→ Start a conversation with someone]]
[[→ Stay silent and pretend to be busy]]



:: Your heart skips a beat. {"position":"300,900","size":"100,100"}
You barely know the person next to you. You exchanged a few rushed whispers, trying to remember details. When it’s your turn, you stand up, feeling everyone's attention shifting towards you. 

''What will you do?''
<img src="pic 1.png" style= " max-width:350px; ">
[[→ Introduce yourself confidently]]
[[→ Introduce yourself with humor]]



:: → Become the leader {"position":"475,1550","size":"100,100"}
<img src="pic 14.png" style= " max-width:350px; ">
You took the initiative and asked, “Do you guys mind if I become the leader?” Everyone agreed with it only because they wanted to avoid being the leader. You started dividing the work among your teammates, and your group presentation went well. 

[[The bell rings]] 


:: → Break the ice {"position":"150,1550","size":"100,100"}
<img src="pic 12.png" style= " max-width:350px; ">
You turn to your group and awkwardly say, “Hi… I guess we are a group now.” Your group laughs, then the others start talking too. The conversation starts slowly, but it starts.

[[The bell rings]]


:: → Get up early and get ready for school {"position":"200,500","size":"100,100"}
<img src="pic 2.png" style= " max-width:350px; ">
You get up directly from your bed and start getting ready for school without rushing. You have plenty of time to double-check your bags, eat your breakfast properly, and leave the house. As you head towards the school, your head feels calm and clear, though you feel a little nervous. 

When you reach school, it’s still very early. Even too early, the classrooms are very empty, and only a few students are around. You sit near the hallway, scrolling through your phone, pretending to be busy to ignore the awkwardness the silence feels. You thought arriving earlier would make things easier, but instead, it gives you more time to overthink. 

[[You took a glance around your classroom]]


:: → Introduce yourself confidently {"position":"200,1000","size":"100,100"}
<img src="pic 8.PNG" style= " max-width:350px; ">
You stood up confidently and started talking. “Hello everyone, my name is Sunli, I’m looking forward to meeting you all this year.” The teacher nodded approvingly and continued to the next student. 

[[You listened and waited until everyone has finished with their introduction.]]




:: → Introduce yourself with humor {"position":"400,1000","size":"100,100"}
<img src="pic 9.PNG" style= " max-width:350px; ">
You stand up and smile awkwardly. “Uh… Hi, I’m Sunli, and I swear I’m more interesting than my introduction.”  A few people giggle, and someone even laughs. The tension in the room eases a lot as you sit back down

[[You listened and waited until everyone has finished with their introduction.]] 


:: → Let it happen naturally {"position":"300,1550","size":"100,100"}
<img src="pic 13.png" style= " max-width:350px; ">
You sit down with your group and listen as others begin talking first. Someone asks, “So.. Who wants to do what?”, you immediately take your chance and add your part to the conversation. You start quietly, but slowly get involved.

[[The bell rings]] 


:: → Snooze your alarm and sleep for a little longer {"position":"400,500","size":"100,100"}
<img src="pic 3.png" style= " max-width:350px; ">
You turn off your alarm and close your eyes again. Somehow, when you wake up again, the panic you expected doesn’t come. You’re not late, but just on time. You rush to prepare a little, but not enough to feel overwhelmed. You head towards school.

When you arrive, the building is already alive. Students are everywhere, talking, laughing, and complaining about their classes and schedules. Everywhere you look, you see new faces. You blend with the crowd and walk into your classroom. You feel a sense of comfort in not standing out. 

[[You took a glance around your classroom]] 


:: → Start a conversation with someone {"position":"200,700","size":"100,100"}
<img src="pic 5.png" style= " max-width:350px; ">
You look around at the people sitting near you. After a moment's hesitation, you muster the courage to speak to the person. You walked over and asked something simple, maybe even too simple. “Hey… is this class confusing for you too?” 

They laughed, relieved. The conversations start awkwardly, but they don’t stay that way for long. You talk about schedules, teachers, and how weird the first day always feels. It’s not a deep connection, but it’s something. For the rest of the lesson, the classroom feels a bit warmer. 

[[You heard footsteps]]


:: → Stay silent and pretend to be busy {"position":"400,700","size":"100,100"}
<img src="pic 6.png" style= " max-width:350px; ">
You stay silent and stare at your phone pretending to be busy, but you're actually just looking at your lock screen. You pull out your notebook, flipping through pages with no purpose. It’s not like you don’t want to talk to anyone; you’re just scared of making things awkward.

Someone eventually asks you a small question anyway. You answer briefly. It’s not a huge moment, but it reminds you that being quiet doesn’t mean being invisible.

[[You heard footsteps]] 


